$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure To Synthesize Compounds of Formula 9.
3-(6-Chloro-5-(E)-styrylpyridin-3-yl)pyridine. To a reaction vessel in a
nitrogen atmosphere containing 5-bromo-2-chloro-3-(E)-styrylpyridine (5;
1.5 g, 5.08 mmol) were added pyridin-3-yl boronic acid (781 mg, 6.35
mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (5% mol), and Na2CO3 (2.5
equiv) in 1,4-dioxane. The mixture was stirred at reflux for 24 h,
followed by TLC. The product was cooled to room temperature and filtered
on Celite. The solution was dried on MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated. The
residue was purified by chromatography (c-hexane/ ethylacetate= 7:3), The
title compound (1.41g) as a pale yellow solid (95% yield). Mp: 159°C. IR
(KBr disc): 3045, 3019, 2924, 2853, 1638, 1578, 1446, 1427, 1385, 1166,
1087, 1057, 1023, 951, 921, 804, 729, 714, 687 cm-1. 1H NMR(CDCl3): δ
8.88(d, 1H, J= 2.2Hz), 8, 71-8.69 (dd, 1H, J = 1.7 Hz, J = 4.76 Hz), 8.49
(d, 1H, J = 2.3 Hz), 8.14 (d, 1H, J = 2.3Hz), 7.94-7.91(m, 1H), 7.58(d,
2H, J= 7.3Hz), 7.40-7.26 (m, 5H), 7.13 (d, 1H, J = 16.4 Hz, CH=CH). 13C
NMR (CDCl3): δ 149.92, 149.70, 148.10, 146.09, 136.15, 136.10, 134.49,
133.99, 133.04, 132.91, 132.53, 132.30, 128.89 (2C), 127.06 (2C), 123.86,
122.72. LCMS(EI): 293.35 [M + H+], 295.34 [M+ + 2].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM First Evidence That Oligopyridines, α-Helix Foldamers, Inhibit Mcl-1 and
Sensitize Ovarian Carcinoma Cells to Bcl-xL-Targeting Strategies
